          Executive Summary: The Fundamental Difference
        </div>
        <ul class="callout-list">
          <li><strong>The Price Gap:</strong> For an identical $500,000 death benefit, whole life insurance costs between <strong>6 to 10 times more per month</strong> than a 20-year level term policy ($32/mo vs. $360/mo for a healthy 35-year-old).</li>
          <li><strong>Lapse & Surrender Reality:</strong> According to Society of Actuaries (SOA) industry studies, more than <strong>40% of whole life policies are surrendered or lapse within the first 10 years</strong>, resulting in substantial financial losses for policyholders due to upfront agent commissions and surrender charges.</li>
          <li><strong>The Recommended Financial Strategy:</strong> For 95% of American households, purchasing a 20- or 30-year level term policy and investing the premium savings in low-cost index funds ("Buy Term and Invest the Difference") builds dramatically higher net worth.</li>
