      <p class="lead-text">
        Few consumer financial products generate as much aggressive sales marketing and consumer confusion as life insurance. Insurance agents often market whole life policies as "wealth-building vehicles" and "personal banking systems," while fee-only fiduciary financial advisors strongly favor straightforward term life contracts. Understanding the mathematical realities beneath these contracts is vital.
      </p>

